title: Biblical Election According to the KJV
description: What the King James text actually says about election: who is chosen, for what purpose, on what condition, what they are urged to do, and what cuts them off.
output: lessons/heresies/election-in-the-bible.html

# Converted from the hand-made chart page lessons/heresies/election-in-the-bible.html (one 5-column table, 14 rows).
# The table is split by column so each slide fits at 390 px: purpose, condition, what the elect are urged to do, what cuts off,
# each in three slides of rows 1-5, 6-10 and 11-14. The long verse quotes in the old "condition" column are now scripture
# blocks (full KJV verses, pulled by the builder), with the author's "in him" highlight kept.

=== Election in Scripture
--- Biblical Election According to the KJV [title]
overline: What the Text Actually Says
heading: Biblical Election According to the KJV
sub: Election in Scripture means being singled out by God for a special purpose, privilege, or service.
center: It is never presented as God choosing who will believe or be caused to be saved.
center: It is always accompanied by responsibilities and, in many cases, warnings of real consequences for failure.

=== The chart: stated purpose
--- Stated purpose (1 of 3)
kicker: Group / Reference
table: Group / Reference | Stated Purpose
tr: **Israel as a nation** [[Deuteronomy 7:6-8]] | To be a special people unto the {Lord}, a holy people, above all people upon the face of the earth; to receive the covenant promises and the land
tr: **Angels** [[1 Timothy 5:21]] | To remain in their holy office and serve as witnesses before God
tr: **Christ Himself** [[Isaiah 42:1-4]] (quoted in [[Matthew 12:18]]) | To bring forth judgment to the Gentiles, establish justice upon earth, be a light and covenant to the people
tr: **Believers** [[Romans 8:28-33]] | To be conformed to the image of His Son; to be justified and glorified
tr: **Believers** [[Ephesians 1:4-5]] | To be holy and without blame before Him in love; unto the adoption of children (full heirship at the redemption of the body)

--- Stated purpose (2 of 3)
kicker: Group / Reference
table: Group / Reference | Stated Purpose
tr: **Believers** [[Colossians 3:12]] | To put on mercies, kindness, humbleness, meekness, longsuffering, forbearing, forgiving, and charity (love)
tr: **Believers** [[1 Thessalonians 1:4]] | To receive the gospel in power and serve the living and true God; to be ensamples to others
tr: **Believers** [[2 Thessalonians 2:13]] | To the full obtaining of salvation through sanctification of the Spirit and belief of the truth; to obtain the glory of our Lord Jesus Christ
tr: **Believers** [[2 Timothy 2:10]] | To the full obtaining of salvation which is in Christ Jesus with eternal glory
tr: **Believers** [[Titus 1:1]] | Acknowledging of the truth which is after godliness; in hope of eternal life

--- Stated purpose (3 of 3)
kicker: Group / Reference
table: Group / Reference | Stated Purpose
tr: **Believers** [[1 Peter 1:1-2]] | Unto obedience and sprinkling of the blood of Jesus Christ
tr: **Believers/Church** [[1 Peter 2:9]] | That ye should shew forth the praises of Him who hath called you out of darkness into His marvellous light
tr: **Believers** [[Matthew 24:22]], [[Matthew 24:24]], [[Matthew 24:31]] (parallels Mark 13:20, 22, 27) | Days of tribulation shortened for the sake of believers who are in Christ; to be gathered from the four winds after the tribulation
tr: **Elect lady and sister** [[2 John 1]], [[2 John 13]] | To walk in truth and love; abide in the doctrine of Christ

=== The chart: stated or implied condition
--- Stated or implied condition (1 of 3)
kicker: Group / Reference
table: Group / Reference | Stated or Implied Condition
tr: **Israel** Deut 7:6–8 | The {Lord}’s love and the oath He sware unto the fathers (v. 8); expressly not because of their numbers or righteousness (v. 7; cf. Deut 9:4–6)
tr: **Angels** 1 Tim 5:21 | Did not join the rebellion (implied by contrast with fallen angels in 2 Pet 2:4; Jude 6)
tr: **Christ** Isa 42:1–4 | God’s delight in Him; Spirit placed upon Him (Isa 42:1)
tr: **Believers** Rom 8:28–33 | Those who love God and are the called according to His purpose (v. 28)
tr: **Believers** Eph 1:4–5 | All those who are **IN HIM**; chosen **in Him** before the foundation of the world; according to the good pleasure of His will (v. 5)

--- Stated or implied condition (2 of 3)
kicker: Group / Reference
table: Group / Reference | Stated or Implied Condition
tr: **Believers** Col 3:12 | Already addressed as “elect of God, holy and beloved” (v. 12)
tr: **Believers** 1 Thess 1:4 | Evident by their work of faith, labour of love, patience of hope; gospel came in much assurance and joy of the Holy Ghost (vv. 3–6)
tr: **Believers** 2 Thess 2:13 | Already believing the truth; through ongoing sanctification of the Spirit (v. 13)
tr: **Believers** 2 Tim 2:10 | Those for whom Paul endures: all the elect who will obtain the completion of salvation through the preached gospel
tr: **Believers** Titus 1:1 | Already possess the faith common to God’s elect and knowledge of the truth (v. 1)

--- Stated or implied condition (3 of 3)
kicker: Group / Reference
table: Group / Reference | Stated or Implied Condition
tr: **Believers** 1 Pet 1:1–2 | According to the foreknowledge of God the Father, through sanctification of the Spirit (v. 2)
tr: **Believers/Church** 1 Pet 2:9 | Mercy obtained (v. 10); contrast with those who stumble at the word being disobedient (vv. 7–8)
tr: **Believers** Matt 24:22, 24, 31 | Believers already in Christ; simply called “the elect”
tr: **Elect lady and sister** 2 John 1, 13 | Some of her children walking in truth (v. 4)

=== The chart: what the elect are urged to do
--- What the elect are called or urged to do (1 of 3)
kicker: Group / Reference
table: Group / Reference | What the Elect Are Called/Urged to Do
tr: **Israel** Deut 7:6–8 | Keep His commandments, love Him, serve Him with all heart and soul, walk in His ways (Deut 10:12–13; 11:22)
tr: **Angels** 1 Tim 5:21 | Continue in obedience and holiness
tr: **Christ** Isa 42:1–4 | Perfect faithfulness and obedience (He shall not fail nor be discouraged, v. 4)
tr: **Believers** Rom 8:28–33 | Love God (v. 28); continue in the process leading to glorification
tr: **Believers** Eph 1:4–5 | Be holy and without blame in love; walk worthy of the vocation wherewith ye are called (Eph 4:1; broader letter)

--- What the elect are called or urged to do (2 of 3)
kicker: Group / Reference
table: Group / Reference | What the Elect Are Called/Urged to Do
tr: **Believers** Col 3:12 | Put on the listed virtues; let the peace of God rule in hearts; be thankful (vv. 12–15)
tr: **Believers** 1 Thess 1:4 | Wait for His Son from heaven; continue as ensamples (vv. 7–10)
tr: **Believers** 2 Thess 2:13 | Stand fast and hold the traditions taught (v. 15)
tr: **Believers** 2 Tim 2:10 | Endure suffering, continue in the things learned (2 Tim 3:14); if we suffer we shall reign, if we deny Him He will deny us (2:11–13)
tr: **Believers** Titus 1:1 | Live godly lives consistent with the truth; rebuke false professors (vv. 9–16)

--- What the elect are called or urged to do (3 of 3)
kicker: Group / Reference
table: Group / Reference | What the Elect Are Called/Urged to Do
tr: **Believers** 1 Pet 1:1–2 | Be holy in all manner of conversation (1:15); purify souls by obeying the truth (1:22); gird up minds, be sober, hope to the end (1:13)
tr: **Believers/Church** 1 Pet 2:9 | Abstain from fleshly lusts, have honest conversation among the Gentiles (2:11–12); submit to ordinances (2:13ff)
tr: **Believers** Matt 24:22, 24, 31 | Watch, pray always, endure unto the end (broader discourse, Matt 24:13, 42–44; Mark 13:33–37)
tr: **Elect lady and sister** 2 John 1, 13 | Walk in love, keep His commandments (vv. 5–6); abide in the doctrine of Christ (v. 9); refuse to receive false teachers (vv. 10–11)

=== The chart: what disqualifies or cuts off
--- What disqualifies or cuts off (1 of 3)
kicker: Group / Reference
table: Group / Reference | What Disqualifies or Cuts Off
tr: **Israel** Deut 7:6–8 | Breaking the covenant, idolatry, disobedience → curses, removal from the land, being cut off (Deut 28:15–68; 29:25–28; 30:17–18)
tr: **Angels** 1 Tim 5:21 | Rebellion → cast down, chained in darkness (2 Pet 2:4; Jude 6)
tr: **Christ** Isa 42:1–4 | None possible; He is perfect
tr: **Believers** Rom 8:28–33 | None explicitly stated in this passage
tr: **Believers** Eph 1:4–5 | Grieve not the holy Spirit of God, whereby ye are sealed unto the day of redemption (Eph 4:30)

--- What disqualifies or cuts off (2 of 3)
kicker: Group / Reference
table: Group / Reference | What Disqualifies or Cuts Off
tr: **Believers** Col 3:12 | Context warns against being beguiled by false teaching and not holding the Head (Col 2:8, 18–19)
tr: **Believers** 1 Thess 1:4 | None explicit in immediate context; broader letter warns against uncleanness (4:3–7)
tr: **Believers** 2 Thess 2:13 | Broader context warns of not loving the truth leading to strong delusion (vv. 10–12)
tr: **Believers** 2 Tim 2:10 | Denying Him → He will deny us (v. 12)
tr: **Believers** Titus 1:1 | Professing to know God but denying Him in works → reprobate (v. 16)

--- What disqualifies or cuts off (3 of 3)
kicker: Group / Reference
table: Group / Reference | What Disqualifies or Cuts Off
tr: **Believers** 1 Pet 1:1–2 | None explicitly in vv. 1–2, but broader letter warns against returning to former lusts and false teachers
tr: **Believers/Church** 1 Pet 2:9 | Disobedience leads to stumbling and appointment to judgment (v. 8, by contrast)
tr: **Believers** Matt 24:22, 24, 31 | Warned of possible deception by false christs and prophets (if it were possible, they shall deceive the very elect, v. 24)
tr: **Elect lady and sister** 2 John 1, 13 | Transgressing and not abiding in the doctrine of Christ → hath not God (v. 9); receiving false teachers → partaker in their evil deeds (v. 11)

